From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: let the tc matchall police reach the RX meter

airoha_tc_matchall_act_validate() refuses a police action when any of
peakrate, avrate, overhead or mtu is set.  tc cannot build a police
action without an mtu: act_police copies parm->mtu into tcfp_mtu and,
when the user leaves it unset, replaces the zero with ~0 or the
rate-table cell size before the action is stored
(net/sched/act_police.c:168-172).  The flow action then copies that
field into entry->police.mtu (:465), so the last term is true for every
police action and matchall police is rejected with -EOPNOTSUPP before
airoha_qdma_set_rx_meter() runs.

Drop the mtu term and keep the peakrate/avrate/overhead refusals; the
RX meter sizes its bucket from rate and burst alone.  peakrate stays in
the message because this path still rejects it, unlike the flower path
where 99991 has a separate peakrate branch and a shorter string.

The 7.4 and 7.3 queues apply this hunk with -F0 and no fuzz.  Not run
on a device.

Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3979,10 +3979,15 @@
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	}
 
+	/* act_police fills an unset tcfp_mtu with ~0 or the rate-table cell
+	 * size before the action is stored, so testing it here refuses every
+	 * police action tc can build; the RX meter sizes its bucket from rate
+	 * and burst alone.
+	 */
 	if (act->police.peakrate_bytes_ps || act->police.avrate ||
-	    act->police.overhead || act->police.mtu) {
+	    act->police.overhead) {
 		NL_SET_ERR_MSG_MOD(f->common.extack,
-				   "peakrate/avrate/overhead/mtu unsupported");
+				   "peakrate/avrate/overhead police is not supported");
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	}
 
